Z||000007||phillip||04-07-2000||07:05 AM||||i'm wondering about that. ACE says use a manual tranny only for light duty or show car purposes. v8 archie says stick any fiero tranny behind a similar output small block, no problems. suposivly, northstars are "tourque phased" (something to do with reducing tourque steer on front wheel drive) and should have lower tourque ratings than similar output smallblocks (info out of a kit car mag.). is ACE being overly cautious or is v8 archie taking a risk? the available info's contradictory. can the manual tranny v8 owners (SB and/or northstar) offer experience/opinions? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||04-07-2000||07:24 AM||||The people at ACE are heavy into racing which means that their definition of light duty might be different than ours.||||reg||1
